  {
   "text": "I built the headphone hook as a design, but it is not sliced or sent to the P1S, since you asked for the part only.\n\nThe hook is a 50 x 30 x 4 mm mount plate with a 40 mm wide J-hook rising 24 mm, curling over the top to 42 mm total height. The hook has a 14 mm outer radius. Two M4 countersunk holes (4.5 mm shaft, 8.5 mm head, 90 degrees) are 30 mm apart. You didn't name a screw, so I used M4 as the default, and every size is a guess from common values.\n\nI moved the holes 8 mm forward of the centerline so the countersinks clear the hook post. The geometry checks out: the body is 50 x 41 x 42 mm, watertight, with 2 mm minimum walls and both hole diameters correct. The one failed check is the step count (6 built against 3 planned), because the holes were added as separate steps. That's a construction detail, not a flaw in the part, but I've left it failed rather than call it done.\n\nNext step: tell me the screw you'll use if it isn't M4, and I'll resize the countersinks. Or say the word and I'll slice it on the P1S in PLA."
